    "concept": "Secondary Storage - Hard Disk Pack Capacity & Sector Addressing",
    "markdown": "- **Givens & Disk Geometry:**\n  - Number of recording surfaces $= 16 = 2^4$\n  - Number of tracks per surface $= 128 = 2^7$\n  - Number of sectors per track $= 256 = 2^8$\n  - Sector capacity $= 512\\text{ bytes} = 2^9\\text{ bytes}$\n\n- **Calculations:**\n  - **Total Number of Sectors in the Disk Pack:**\n    $$\\text{Total Sectors} = \\text{Surfaces} \\times \\text{Tracks/Surface} \\times \\text{Sectors/Track}$$\n    $$\\text{Total Sectors} = 2^4 \\times 2^7 \\times 2^8 = 2^{19}\\text{ sectors}$$\n  - **Bits Required to Specify a Sector:**\n    $$\\text{Address Bits} = \\log_2(2^{19}) = 19\\text{ bits}$$\n  - **Total Disk Pack Capacity:**\n    $$\\text{Capacity} = 2^{19}\\text{ sectors} \\times 512\\text{ bytes/sector} = 2^{19} \\times 2^9\\text{ bytes} = 2^{28}\\text{ bytes}$$\n    $$\\text{Capacity} = \\frac{2^{28}}{2^{20}}\\text{ Mbytes} = 2^8\\text{ Mbytes} = 256\\text{ Mbytes}$$\n\n- **Conclusion:** The disk capacity is $256\\text{ Mbyte}$ and $19\\text{ bits}$ are required to address any sector.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is **Option A ($256\\text{ Mbyte}, 19\\text{ bits}$)**.",
