    "markdown": "- **Givens & Structural Rules:**\n  - $B^+$ tree where each node holds at most $2$ keys and $3$ child links (order $p = 3$).\n  - Initial tree structure contains keys: $10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60$.\n  - Insertions in order: $K15$, then $K25$.\n\n- **Insertion Step Trace:**\n  - **1. Insert $K15$:**\n    - Leaf node $[10, 20]$ overflows on inserting $15 \\implies [10, 15, 20]$.\n    - Splits into $[10]$ and $[15, 20]$, pushing key $15$ to the parent node.\n  - **2. Insert $K25$:**\n    - Leaf node $[20, 30]$ overflows on inserting $25 \\implies [20, 25, 30]$.\n    - Splits into $[20]$ and $[25, 30]$, pushing key $25$ up.\n    - Subsequent internal splits propagate.\n  - Inspecting the four candidate node configurations given in the question:\n    - Only exactly $1$ of the depicted candidate nodes matches the resulting $B^+$ tree node state.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is **Option A ($1$)**.",
