    "concept": "File Organization & Indexing - B+ Tree Key Deletion & Merging",
    "markdown": "- **Deletion of Key $K50$:**\n  - Starting from the $B^+$ tree obtained after inserting $K15$ and $K25$, key $K50$ is deleted from its leaf node.\n  - Underflow occurs in the leaf node containing $50$.\n  - Borrowing / redistributing from adjacent sibling nodes or merging nodes is performed according to $B^+$ tree deletion invariants.\n\n- **Evaluating Statements:**\n  - **Statement (i):** *\"The height of the tree remains the same.\"*\n    - **True.** The deletion of key $50$ causes local merging/borrowing among sibling leaf nodes without shrinking the root node or reducing the overall height of the tree.\n  - **Statement (ii):** *\"The specified node is present in the tree.\"*\n    - **True.** The resulting internal node structure retains the referenced node content.\n  - **Statement (iii):** *\"The root node remains unchanged.\"*\n    - **False.** The key values in the root/internal nodes are updated to reflect the new split keys following deletion.\n  - Therefore, statements (i) and (ii) are true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is **Option A (Statements (i) and (ii) are true)**.",
